        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(media): support configurable containerWorkdir in sandbox media path normalization (#98446)",
        "body": "Fixes #98446.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenShell containers use `/sandbox` as their container-side workspace root, but `resolveSandboxedMediaSource` was hardcoded to recognize only `/workspace` paths. When an agent running in an OpenShell sandbox generates media under `/sandbox/output/photo.png` and tries to send it out, the path is rejected:\n\n```\nPath escapes sandbox root: /sandbox/output/photo.png\n```\n\nThis happens because the container path mapper only checks against the hardcoded `/workspace` prefix — anything under `/sandbox` falls through to the sandbox-root boundary check and gets rejected.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nParameterized the container workspace root so sandbox backends can supply their own value instead of defaulting to `/workspace`. Changes:\n\n- `resolveSandboxedMediaSource`, `mapContainerWorkspaceFileUrl`, `mapContainerWorkspacePath` accept optional `containerWorkdir` (default `/workspace`)\n- `AttachmentMediaPolicy` carries `containerWorkdir` through message action and reply media normalization\n- `reply-media-paths.ts` reads it from `ensureSandboxWorkspaceForSession`\n- Trailing slashes normalized before prefix checks (`/sandbox/` → `/sandbox`)\n\nNo OpenShell plugin security boundary (`/sandbox`, `/agent` only) is changed.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Reproduction on current main** (BEFORE fix, containerWorkdir defaults to /workspace):\n\n```\n=== BEFORE (default /workspace) ===\n  REJECTED: file:///sandbox/output/photo.png — Path escapes sandbox root\n  REJECTED: /sandbox/output/photo.png — Path escapes sandbox root\n```\n\n**After this patch** (containerWorkdir=\"/sandbox\"):\n\n```\n=== AFTER (containerWorkdir=/sandbox) ===\n  ALLOWED: file:///sandbox/output/photo.png → sandbox-root/output/photo.png\n  ALLOWED: /sandbox/output/photo.png → sandbox-root/output/photo.png\n  ALLOWED: /sandbox/secret/token → sandbox-root/secret/token\n\n=== Negative control (/sandboxer/secret — prefix attack) ===\n  REJECTED: /sandboxer/secret — Path escapes sandbox root\n```\n\n**Real environment tested**: Linux, Node 22.19+, local source checkout, real temp directories.\n\n**Unit tests**:\n\n```\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/sandbox-paths.test.ts --run\n Test Files  1 passed (1) / Tests  41 passed (41)\n\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/outbound/message-action-params.test.ts --run\n Test Files  1 passed (1) / Tests  34 passed (34)\n\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/auto-reply/reply/reply-media-paths.test.ts --run\n Test Files  1 passed (1) / Tests  23 passed (23)\n\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/tools/message-tool.test.ts --run\n Test Files  1 passed (1) / Tests  113 passed (113)\n```\n\nTotal: 4 test files, 211 tests passed.\n\n**Lint**: `node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs` on all changed files — exit 0.\n\n**Observed result after fix**: OpenShell `/sandbox/...` media paths correctly resolve; Docker `/workspace` default unchanged; prefix-based attacks (`/sandboxer/secret`) still rejected; trailing-slash workdir configs normalized.\n\n**What was not tested**: Live Kubernetes-deployed OpenShell pod. The proof exercises the same production helper (`resolveSandboxedMediaSource`) and reply normalizer used by the real gateway flow.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`SANDBOX_CONTAINER_WORKDIR` at `sandbox-paths.ts:23` was hardcoded to `/workspace`. The container path mapping helpers used this constant exclusively, so the `mapContainerWorkspaceFileUrl` and `mapContainerWorkspacePath` helpers never matched paths starting with `/sandbox`. The fix parameterizes the workdir so backends can supply their own value.\n\n## AI Assistance\n\n- **AI-assisted**: Yes\n- **Model used**: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)\n- **Co-Authored-By**: Already in commit message\n",
